      "text": "First, we note that both roots lie on the unit circle in the complex plane.  That means that\n\\[|v+w|^2=v^2+w^2+2\\operatorname{Re}(v\\overline{w})=(1+v\\overline{v})+(1+w\\overline{w})+2\\operatorname{Re}(v\\overline{w}) = 2 + 2\\operatorname{Re}(v\\overline{w}).\\]However, the largest possible value for $\\operatorname{Re}(v\\overline{w})$ is 1 (when $v\\overline{w}=1$), so the largest possible value for $|v+w|$ is $\\sqrt{3}.$  Furthermore, $|v+w|\\geq 1$ for any two numbers on the unit circle.  Hence, $\\operatorname{Re}(v\\overline{w})\\leq \\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2},$ so our probability that $\\operatorname{Re}(v\\overline{w})\\geq \\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{4}$ is $$\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{4}}{1}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{4}.$$",
