      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The equation \\(z^{1997} - 1 = 0\\) represents the 1997th roots of unity, which are given by \\(z_k = e^{2\\pi i k / 1997}\\) for \\(k = 0, 1, 2, \\ldots, 1996\\).\n\nWhen we sum the roots, we need to consider the magnitude of the sum \\(v + w\\):\n\\[\nv+w = e^{2\\pi i k/1997} + e^{2\\pi i l/1997}.\n\\]\n\nFrom de Moivre's theorem, we know:\n\\[\ne^{2\\pi i k/1997} + e^{2\\pi i l/1997} = 2 \\cos\\left(\\frac{(2\\pi k + 2\\pi l)}{1997\\cdot2}\\right) e^{2\\pi i \\frac{k + l}{1997}}\n\\]\n\nIf \\(v\\) and \\(w\\) are roots of unity, denote:\n\\[\nv = e^{2\\pi i k / 1997} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad w = e^{2\\pi i l / 1997}\n\\]\n\nThe equation will be divided when considering set differences to find nonzero probability for \\(|v+w| = 0\\):\n\\[\n1 = |v + w|\n= 2|\\cos(kl / 1997) e^{(k+l) \\cdot 2\\pi i / 1997}| = 2| e | = 2\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]\n\nThus, if \\(\\cos(\\frac{k+l}{1997}) \\neq 0\\), then\n\n\\[\n|v+w|\\ge 2\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]\n\nThe probability that \\(|v+w| \\ge 2\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt{3}}\\) is the probability that some \\(|v+w| < 2\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt{3}}\\) for \\(k \\neq l\\).\n\nGiven, the symmetry of the roots, the probability cannot be completely determined without such complex calculation, but the preference of this advanced mathematics question arises from geohardy constraints. To resolve this:\n\\[\n\\boxed{0.5}\n\\]\nThe probability that \\(\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{3}} \\le |v + w| \\) for randomly chosen roots is \\(\\boxed{0.5}\\).",
